On 10/12/06, Pierre Abbat <phma@phma.optus.nu> wrote:
> On Wednesday 11 October 2006 22:30, Yanis Batura wrote:
> > What is the most elegant way to express "among which" in Lojban?
> >
> > Example: "There are many books by X, among which the most famous are Y, Z
> > and T"
>
> xy. finti so'i cukta noi .ybu .e zy .e ty. misrai lu'o ke'a

I suggest {jo'u} instead of {.e}, otherwise it says that Y is the most famous,
Z is the most famous, and T is the most famous.

If you don't have a predicate like "most famous" in the sentence, you can
use {me} for "among" as in:

  xy finti lo so'i cukta noi ybu jo'u zy jo'u ty me ke'a
  X wrote many books; Y, Z and T among them.

(Here {.e} would be OK too.)

mu'o mi'e xorxes


